<title>USA: Genset seeks prostate cancer gene patent.</title>
<headline>Genset seeks prostate cancer gene patent.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Genset said Monday it found several chromosomal regions containing suspected genes linked to prostate cancer, and that it applied for a patent covering its discoveries.</p>
<p>The company said it applied for the patent on November 21.</p>
<p>The discoveries are Genset's first in its prostate cancer gene discovery program, it said, which began about seven months ago.</p>
<p>Genset is collaborating with France's Synthelabo in the prostate cancer gene discovery program.</p>
